   scoped to the four sites, or 8.8 with the class-level scope written into the
   description - the owner should pick one and keep the description and the score
   consistent.

   WHAT THE FIX DOES. The four sites use the project's established idiom - quote()
   for values, intval()/casts for numeric ids - and the sweep applies it to the
   same anti-pattern tree-wide, with a validated-identifier helper (SqlIdent) for
   schema and column names, which cannot be bound as parameters. Because a fix
   for today's omission does not stop tomorrow's, the relay is additionally
   deny-by-default against data/config/relay-allowlist.php (4.1), and a static
   gate (make security-check) now fails the build when a raw concatenation is
   reintroduced into an application file.

   3.3 FINDING 3 - vcalendar.php pass-the-hash and cross-provider access
       (CWE-287 / CWE-836 / CWE-639), CVSS 3.1

   MECHANISM. freemed_get_auth() (pre-fix vcalendar.php:66-71) authenticated a
   request by comparing the request-supplied hash parameter against the stored
   value directly, in SQL:
       ... WHERE username='".addslashes($_GET['user'])."' AND
                 userpassword='".addslashes($_GET['hash'])."'
   The stored user.userpassword is an unsalted MD5 digest of the password, so the
   digest WAS the credential: anyone who could read it - a database read, a
   backup, a log, or the SQL injection in 3.2 - could authenticate with it
   without knowing the password. A GET parameter carrying a credential also lands
   in access logs and in the endpoint's own syslog line
   (vcalendar.php:63 logged the username for an unauthenticated request).
   Separately, the provider was taken from $_REQUEST['physician'] with no check
   against the caller, so any authenticated caller could name any physician.

   MEASURED EVIDENCE - the authentication bypass, live, register_argc_argv = Off
   (vcalendar-auth.txt section 1; the harness pre-fix base is commit 8938de83).

     CASE anonymous                        HTTP 200, text/html, 964 bytes
       body ends: Fatal error: Uncaught Error: Call to undefined function
                  prepare() in /var/www/html/vcalendar.php:62
       (no 401 challenge at all before the fix)
       syslog: "vCalendar [get] username =" (empty)

     CASE get-hash, non-physician account + CORRECT digest
                                           HTTP 200, text/html, 377 bytes
       body ends: "Not enough information provided."
       -> authentication SUCCEEDED, and execution then stopped at the provider
          check exactly as designed.
       syslog: "vCalendar [get] username = clerk"

     CASE get-hash, admin account + CORRECT digest
                                           HTTP 200, text/html, 1809 bytes
       body: Physician/FreemedDb warnings ending in
             Fatal error: Uncaught TypeError: count(): Argument #1 ($value) must
             be of type Countable|array, null given in
             .../core/Physician.class.php:93
       -> authentication SUCCEEDED; the endpoint then failed for want of a seeded
          physician row.
       syslog: "vCalendar [get] username = admin"

     CASE get-hash, admin account + IMPOSSIBLE digest
                                           HTTP 200, text/html, 625 bytes
       body ends in the same prepare() fatal inside freemed_basic_auth()
       -> NOT authenticated.

     Three distinguishable outcomes for three credentials: the digest is the
     credential. (The digest was confirmed to match the stored userpassword out of
     band by a direct SQL comparison returning a row count of 1 for that account
     and 0 for the impossible digest - never by printing the digest.)

